# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/romance/lyra_tobias.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lyra_second_place
# en: Second Place, Again
title [66b03a] = 又是第二
# en: The rankings are up. {~Your name is above hers, by one mark. Lyra stands in front of the list with her arms folded. "One mark," she says. "I'll have it back by Frostcall."|Her name is above yours, by one mark, and she's not looking at it. She's looking at you. "One mark," she says. "I'll make it two by Frostcall."|Your names are level. The registrar has had to put you side by side, alphabetically, and she hates it. "A tie," she says, arms folded. "I'll break it by Frostcall."}
text [1e371d] = 排名贴出来了。{~你的名字在她上面，只差一分。莱拉抱着胳膊站在榜前。“一分，”她说，“霜唤月之前我会拿回来。”|她的名字在你上面，只差一分，可她没在看榜。她在看你。“一分，”她说，“霜唤月之前我会让它变成两分。”|你们俩分数相同。教务只好按字母顺序把你们并排列出，她恨透了这一点。“平手，”她抱着胳膊说，“霜唤月之前我会打破它。”}
# en: A posted list of class rankings on a stone wall, two names at the top, a red-haired girl staring at the second one.
scene [4d01ab] = 石墙上贴着一张班级排名，榜首两个名字，一个红发女孩盯着第二个。
# en: "You can try."
opt.left.label [a7c127] = “你可以试试。”
# en: {~Her eyes narrow, and something in them lights. "Oh, I will," she says, and walks off already planning. You find yourself studying harder too, which you suspect was the point.|"Good," she says, with relish. "I'd hate to win against someone who wasn't trying." She's almost smiling.|"Try," she repeats, as if tasting the word. She's in the library before you the next morning. So are you.}
opt.left.say.1 [5775c1] = {~她眯起眼睛，眼底有什么亮了起来。“我会的。”她说着走开，已经在盘算了。你发现自己也更用功了——你怀疑这正是她的目的。|“很好，”她津津有味地说，“赢一个不尽力的人，我会觉得没意思。”她几乎在笑。|“试试，”她把这个词重复了一遍，像在品味它。第二天一早她比你先到图书馆。你也到了。}
# en: "It's just a list."
opt.right.label [eddc15] = “不过是张榜。”
# en: {~"It's never just a list," she says, and for a second she sounds about twelve. Then the Vaneshade face comes back. "But you wouldn't know that."|She looks at you as though you'd said the sun was optional. Then she walks away to study.|"Lucky you," she says, and means something you don't catch until later.}
opt.right.say.1 [5c2433] = {~“从来都不只是张榜。”她说，有那么一瞬间，她听上去像个十二岁的孩子。随后凡妮希德家的神情又回来了。“不过你不会懂的。”|她看着你，仿佛你刚说太阳可有可无。然后她走去自习了。|“你真幸运。”她说。这句话的意思，你很久以后才明白。}

@event lyra_glove
# en: The Glove
title [822695] = 手套
# en: Lyra drops a glove at your feet in an empty corridor. An actual glove. "Vaneshades settle things properly," she says. "You've been in my head all term. It's insufferable. Dawn, the practice circle. If I win, you stop." She doesn't say stop what. She's gone red to the ears.
text [33af1c] = 在空无一人的走廊里，莱拉把一只手套丢在你脚边。一只真正的手套。“凡妮希德家用正式的方式解决问题，”她说，“你整个学期都在我脑子里，烦死了。黎明，练习场。我赢了，你就停下。”她没说停下什么。她连耳朵都红了。
# en: A red-haired girl dropping a leather duelling glove at a student's feet in an empty corridor, her chin very high.
scene [0c6174] = 空走廊里，红发女孩把一只皮质决斗手套丢在一个学生脚边，下巴扬得很高。
# en: Pick it up
opt.left.label [b90f6a] = 捡起来
# en: You meet her at dawn. Neither of you casts a single spell. You stand in the frost and talk for an hour instead, about nothing, and she forgets to win, and so do you.
opt.left.say.1 [385f4a] = 黎明时你去见她。你们谁都没施一个咒。你们站在霜里聊了一个钟头，什么都聊，她忘了要赢，你也忘了。
# en: Hand it back, politely
opt.right.label [b4d5ae] = 礼貌地还给她
# en: "You dropped this." Her face does something complicated and then goes perfectly smooth. "So I did," she says, and puts it on, and that's the end of it. Almost.
opt.right.say.1 [a3d9ff] = “你掉了这个。”她的表情复杂地变了几变，然后变得一丝不乱。“是啊，”她说着戴上手套，事情就这样结束了。差不多结束了。

@event lyra_after_hours
# en: After the Torches
title [fa1628] = 火把熄灭之后
# en: {~The duelling hall's torches go out at ten. Lyra lights one flame in her palm and keeps practising.|Lyra is still in the practice hall after the torches are out, working one form over and over.|The torches are out again. Lyra's palm flame is the only light, and she's waiting, as if she knew you'd come.} "You're late," she says. You didn't say you were coming.
text [43d720] = {~决斗厅的火把十点就熄了。莱拉在掌心点起一簇火，继续练。|火把熄了，莱拉还在练习厅里，一遍又一遍地练同一个招式。|火把又熄了。莱拉掌心的火是唯一的光，她在等，好像早知道你会来。}“你迟到了。”她说。你可没说过要来。
# en: An empty practice hall at night, the torches out, a red-haired girl lighting a single flame in her palm so two people can see.
scene [012bc5] = 夜里空荡的练习厅，火把已熄，一个红发女孩在掌心点起一簇火，好让两个人都看得见。
# en: Spar with her
opt.left.label [ca472c] = 陪她对练
# en: {~You spar until your arms shake. She says nothing nice, but she shows you, without explaining, how she shapes the turn of a flame. Then she blows it out, and you walk back in the dark, close enough to bump shoulders.|You spar in the light of her hand. She's better than you. She tells you exactly how, and stays until you've fixed it.|You fight until you're both laughing at a missed block. Lyra doesn't laugh, usually. She stops, surprised at herself.}
opt.left.say.1 [4940bb] = {~你们一直练到你胳膊发抖。她一句好话没说，却不加解释地演示给你看，她是怎样拧转火焰的。然后她吹灭了火，你们在黑暗里走回去，近得肩膀相碰。|你们就着她掌心的光对练。她比你强。她一五一十地告诉你强在哪里，一直留到你改过来。|你们打到两个人都为一次漏挡笑出声。莱拉平时不笑。她停下来，自己也吃了一惊。}
# en: Make her stop
opt.right.label [275e64] = 让她停下
# en: {~"Enough," you say, and take her wrist. The flame goes out. "You'll be useless tomorrow." She glares at you in the dark, and then lets you walk her back, which she almost never does.|You sit on the bench and refuse to move until she does. It takes an hour. Your own reading doesn't get done.|You make her eat something. She eats it as if it's an insult, and then eats yours.}
opt.right.say.1 [09f8aa] = {~“够了。”你说着握住她的手腕。火灭了。“你明天会废掉的。”她在黑暗里瞪着你，然后让你送她回去——她几乎从不这样。|你在长凳上坐下，她不走你就不走。耗了一个钟头。你自己的书一页没看。|你逼她吃点东西。她吃得像受了侮辱，然后把你那份也吃了。}

@event lyra_partner_watch
# en: Burnout Watch
title [a16a07] = 守着她别累垮
# en: You've an arrangement now, the two of you: at midnight, you go and find her, wherever she is, and make her stop. Tonight it's the library. She's on chapter nine of a book with eleven. {~"Two more," she says, without looking up.|"Ten minutes," she says, which means two hours.}
text [83d550] = 你们俩现在有个约定：午夜时，无论她在哪儿，你都去找到她，让她停下。今晚是图书馆。她在读一本十一章的书的第九章。{~“还有两章。”她头也不抬地说。|“十分钟。”她说，意思是两个钟头。}
# en: A candlelit desk buried in books, a red-haired girl asleep on her notes, someone gently taking the quill out of her hand.
scene [f81f92] = 烛光下堆满书的书桌，一个红发女孩趴在笔记上睡着了，有人轻轻从她手里抽走羽毛笔。
# en: Make her stop
opt.left.label [275e64] = 让她停下
# en: {~You close the book on her fingers, gently. She lets you. On the way back she falls asleep against your shoulder, standing up, which you didn't know was possible.|You take the quill. She says something cutting. Then she says thank you, very quietly, as if it costs her a mark.}
opt.left.say.1 [17b628] = {~你轻轻合上书，压住她的手指。她由着你。回去的路上，她站着就靠在你肩上睡着了，你都不知道人还能这样。|你拿走她的羽毛笔。她说了句刻薄话。然后很轻地说了声谢谢，好像这要扣她一分。}
# en: Stay and finish it with her
opt.right.label [908278] = 留下陪她读完
# en: {~You pull up a chair and read chapter ten aloud while she takes notes. By two you're both asleep on the table, and the librarian covers you with a cloak.|You stay. She finishes. She says finishing a book with someone there is a different thing entirely.}
opt.right.say.1 [7aac9d] = {~你拉过一把椅子，把第十章念出来，她记笔记。到两点时，你们俩都趴在桌上睡着了，图书管理员给你们盖上一件斗篷。|你留下了。她读完了。她说，有人在旁边时读完一本书，完全是另一回事。}

@event lyra_not_second
# en: Not Second to Anyone
title [a1c79b] = 不做任何人的第二
# en: Lyra has found out you skipped her match for {~a study group|a club meeting|a friend's crisis}. She is very calm, which is worse than shouting. "I have been second to my mother's ambitions my whole life," she says. {~"I won't be second to a study group."|"I won't be second to a club."|"I know it was a crisis. I know. I still wanted you there."}
text [26f9bd] = 莱拉发现你为了{~一个学习小组|一次社团活动|一个朋友的急事}错过了她的比赛。她非常平静，这比大吼更糟。“我这辈子一直排在我母亲的野心后面，”她说。{~“我不会排在一个学习小组后面。”|“我不会排在一个社团后面。”|“我知道那是急事。我知道。我还是想要你在场。”}
# en: A red-haired girl standing very straight in a corridor, eyes bright with anger, a crumpled tournament list in her fist.
scene [18356e] = 一个红发女孩笔直地站在走廊里，眼里燃着怒火，手里攥着一张揉皱的比赛名单。
# en: Talk it through, properly
opt.left.label [43c9e0] = 好好把话说开
# en: She wants to be argued with, not soothed.
opt.left.hint [10bed1] = 她要的是争辩，不是安抚。
# en: You don't apologise first; you argue. You tell her she's not second, she's the one you'd have fought for a seat beside. She listens. Then she kisses you, angrily, and says next time you'll be in the front row.
opt.left.say.1 [439371] = 你没有先道歉，而是和她争。你告诉她，她不是第二，她是你会为了坐在她身边去争一个位子的人。她听着。然后她吻了你，带着火气，说下次你得坐第一排。
# en: {~Everything you say sounds like an excuse, because it is.|Everything you say sounds like an excuse, because it is.|You were right to go, and you both know it, and somehow that makes it harder to say.} She nods, very correctly, and walks away. She's at your next lecture. She doesn't sit next to you.
opt.left.say.2 [d710db] = {~你说的每句话听上去都像借口，因为它们就是借口。|你说的每句话听上去都像借口，因为它们就是借口。|你去是对的，你们俩都知道，可不知怎么的，这反而更难说出口。}她非常得体地点点头，走了。你下一堂课她也在。她没坐在你旁边。
# en: Apologise, and mean it
opt.right.label [51060b] = 道歉，真心的
# en: "I'm sorry." She looks at you a long time. "Vaneshades don't accept apologies," she says. "But I'm not a Vaneshade with you." It's forgiveness. It still stings, for both of you.
opt.right.say.1 [42a843] = “对不起。”她看了你很久。“凡妮希德家不接受道歉，”她说，“可在你面前，我不是凡妮希德家的人。”这就是原谅了。可你们俩都还隐隐作痛。

@event lyra_empty_chair
# en: Her Mother's Empty Chair
title [d498d5] = 她母亲的空椅子
# en: Lyra's final bout of the year. In the front row of the gallery is a velvet chair with a card on it: "Reserved — Lady Vaneshade." It stays empty. Lyra looks at it once, just before she bows, and then at you.
text [41e532] = 莱拉这一年的最后一场比赛。看台前排有一把天鹅绒椅子，上面放着一张卡片：“预留——凡妮希德夫人。”椅子一直空着。莱拉在行礼前看了它一眼，然后看向你。
# en: A crowded duelling gallery with one empty velvet chair in the front row, a red-haired duellist glancing at it before her bout.
scene [199722] = 坐满人的决斗看台，前排一把空着的天鹅绒椅子，一个红发决斗者在上场前瞥了它一眼。
# en: Sit in the chair
opt.left.label [fad2cc] = 坐到那把椅子上
# en: You walk down to the front and sit in Lady Vaneshade's chair. People stare. Lyra sees, and something in her shoulders lets go. She wins in under a minute. Afterwards she says, "That was a terrible breach of etiquette," and doesn't let go of your hand.
opt.left.say.1 [2ceaf3] = 你走到前排，在凡妮希德夫人的椅子上坐下。人们盯着你看。莱拉看见了，肩膀里有什么松开了。她不到一分钟就赢了。事后她说：“那是严重的失礼。”然后一直没松开你的手。
# en: Cheer louder than anyone
opt.right.label [f04bda] = 喊得比谁都响
# en: You shout her name until the gallery joins in. She doesn't look at the chair again. She wins, and turns, and looks for you, only you, the way she used to look for the scoreboard.
opt.right.say.1 [9b7903] = 你喊她的名字，喊到整个看台都跟着喊。她再没看那把椅子一眼。她赢了，转过身来找你，只找你，就像她从前找记分板那样。

@event lyra_ex
# en: Cold Hearth
title [f78029] = 冷炉
# en: Lyra passes you in the corridor with her chin high and her eyes forward. She's perfectly polite now, which is how you know. A Vaneshade's coldest weapon is good manners.
text [4a4554] = 莱拉在走廊里与你擦肩而过，下巴高扬，目不斜视。她现在对你礼貌周全，你就是从这一点看出来的。凡妮希德家最冷的武器是好教养。
# en: Two people passing in a corridor, one a red-haired girl who keeps her chin high and her eyes forward.
scene [7a80bf] = 两个人在走廊里擦肩而过，其中一个红发女孩下巴高扬，目不斜视。
# en: Let her pass
opt.left.label [bf55e2] = 让她走
# en: She passes. You both keep walking. Behind you, a torch on the wall flares, briefly, as if someone's temper had slipped.
opt.left.say.1 [8a7cd6] = 她走了过去。你们都没停步。你身后，墙上一支火把忽地蹿高了一下，像是谁的脾气没压住。
# en: Say her name
opt.right.label [7e575e] = 叫她的名字
# en: She stops. Turns. "What," she says. You say you miss her as a rival, at least. She almost laughs. "Library," she says. "Thursday. I'll destroy you." It's an olive branch, the Vaneshade way.
opt.right.say.1 [1b7453] = 她停下，转身。“什么事。”她说。你说你想念她这个对手，至少这个。她差点笑出来。“图书馆，”她说，“周四。我会把你打得落花流水。”这是一根橄榄枝，凡妮希德式的。
# en: "Yes?" she says, and waits, and you don't have the words. "I thought not," she says, not unkindly, and goes.
opt.right.say.2 [4ee7c1] = “嗯？”她说，等着，而你找不到话。“我就知道。”她说，并无恶意，然后走了。

@event lyra_partner_neglect
# en: "I Don't Wait"
title [afe1bb] = “我不等人”
# en: Lyra is in your doorway with her arms folded. "I don't wait for people," she says. "I've waited for you three times this month. I counted. I'm a Vaneshade; I count everything." She doesn't say she missed you. She doesn't need to.
text [49941d] = 莱拉抱着胳膊站在你门口。“我不等人，”她说，“这个月我等了你三次。我数过。我是凡妮希德家的人，什么都数。”她没说她想你。她不必说。
# en: A red-haired girl in a duelling coat standing in a doorway with her arms folded, two cups of cold tea on the table behind her.
scene [bc6b4e] = 一个穿决斗外套的红发女孩抱着胳膊站在门口，身后桌上放着两杯凉掉的茶。
# en: "Tomorrow. Dawn. I'll be there first."
opt.left.label [4d7d51] = “明天黎明，我先到。”
# en: You're there first, at dawn, with two cups of tea that are actually hot. She takes one and says nothing, which from her is an embrace.
opt.left.say.1 [834636] = 黎明时你先到了，带着两杯真正热的茶。她接过一杯，什么都没说——对她来说，这就是拥抱。
# en: "You know what term's like."
opt.right.label [b67bf0] = “你知道学期里是什么样。”
# en: "I do," she says. "I manage." She walks away, perfectly upright. It's the most hurt you've ever seen her look.
opt.right.say.1 [afc442] = “我知道，”她说，“我应付得来。”她走开了，背挺得笔直。你从没见过她这么受伤的样子。

@event lyra_lends
# en: A Loan, Vaneshade Style
title [783102] = 凡妮希德式借钱
# en: Lyra would sooner die than borrow. She has noticed, though, that your purse is thin, and she is holding out hers at arm's length without looking at it. "Take what you need," she says. "Don't thank me. Don't ever mention it."
text [ffbd52] = 莱拉宁死也不会向人借钱。不过她注意到你的钱袋瘪了，此刻正把她自己的钱袋伸直胳膊递过来，眼睛不看它。“需要多少拿多少，”她说，“别谢我。永远别提这事。”
# en: A red-haired girl holding out a heavy purse at arm's length, not looking at it, as if it were beneath her notice.
scene [46b429] = 一个红发女孩伸直胳膊递出一只沉甸甸的钱袋，眼睛不看它，好像它不值得她瞧一眼。
# en: Take a little
opt.left.label [5e0faf] = 拿一点
# en: You take a few crowns. She never mentions it again. Neither do you, though you pay her back in study notes she pretends not to read.
opt.left.say.1 [f889cb] = 你拿了几个克朗。她再也没提过。你也没有，不过你用学习笔记还了她，她假装不看。
# en: Refuse, kindly
opt.right.label [3868f0] = 客气地拒绝
# en: "I'm fine." She puts the purse away. "Of course you are," she says, and the next day there's a meal paid for at the village inn in your name.
opt.right.say.1 [7f8f43] = “我没事。”她收起钱袋。“你当然没事。”她说。第二天，镇上的客栈里有一顿饭记在了你的名下，已经付过了。

@event tobias_gerald_approves
# en: Gerald Approves
title [d674c6] = 杰拉尔德认可了
# en: Tobias holds Gerald up to your face. Gerald is wearing {~a new hat|his winter hat}. "He's deciding about you," Tobias says seriously. "He doesn't like everyone. He bit the Verdant Circle's treasurer." Gerald considers you with his small dark eyes.
text [1a7d23] = 托比亚斯把杰拉尔德举到你面前。杰拉尔德戴着{~一顶新帽子|他的冬帽}。“他在考虑你，”托比亚斯严肃地说，“他不是谁都喜欢。他咬过青翠社的司库。”杰拉尔德用一双小小的黑眼睛打量着你。
# en: A large gentle student holding a potted mandrake in a tiny knitted hat up to another student's face, both very solemn.
scene [52fade] = 一个高大温和的学生把一盆戴着小毛线帽的曼德拉草举到另一个学生面前，两人都十分庄重。
# en: Bow to Gerald
opt.left.label [eec4bd] = 向杰拉尔德鞠躬
# en: {~You bow. Gerald screams very softly, which Tobias says is approval. Tobias looks at you as if you'd done something wonderful. You think maybe you have.|You bow, and Gerald pats your nose with a leaf. Tobias goes pink. "He hardly ever does that," he says. "Not even to me."}
opt.left.say.1 [b0af47] = {~你鞠了一躬。杰拉尔德非常轻地尖叫了一声，托比亚斯说这表示认可。他看着你，好像你做了件了不起的事。也许你确实做了。|你鞠了一躬，杰拉尔德用一片叶子拍了拍你的鼻子。托比亚斯脸红了。“他很少这样，”他说，“对我都很少。”}
# en: Offer Gerald a finger
opt.right.label [4a5386] = 伸一根手指给他
# en: {~Gerald bites it. Tobias is mortified and laughs so hard he has to sit down. You're both still laughing when the greenhouse bell goes.|Gerald bites it, then lets go and looks sorry. "He's shy," says Tobias. Your finger disagrees.}
opt.right.say.1 [73864d] = {~杰拉尔德咬了上去。托比亚斯窘得要命，又笑得不得不坐下。温室的钟响时，你们俩还在笑。|杰拉尔德咬了一口，又松开，一副很抱歉的样子。“他害羞。”托比亚斯说。你的手指不同意。}

@event tobias_letter_aloud
# en: Read It to Me
title [e78a93] = 念给我听
# en: Tobias has a letter from home and he hasn't opened it. "My eyes are tired," he says, which isn't true. "Would you read it? Out loud?" It's from his mother. She writes the way people talk on farms: weather first, goats second, love last and briefly.
text [5569ff] = 托比亚斯收到一封家信，还没拆。“我眼睛累了，”他说，这不是真的，“你能念吗？念出声？”信是他母亲写的。她写信的方式就像农场上的人说话：先说天气，再说山羊，爱放在最后，只一句。
# en: A large student sitting on a bench handing another a letter on farm paper, his eyes red-rimmed and tired.
scene [73d0bd] = 一个高大的学生坐在长凳上，把一封写在农场信纸上的信递给另一个人，眼圈发红，满脸疲惫。
# en: Read it, voices and all
opt.left.label [6c58df] = 念，连语气一起
# en: You read it in his mother's voice, as near as you can guess. He laughs at the goats and goes quiet at the end. "She says she's proud," he says. "She never says that." You read that line twice, because he asks.
opt.left.say.1 [d337d5] = 你尽量猜着他母亲的口气念。念到山羊他笑了，念到结尾他安静了。“她说她为我骄傲，”他说，“她从来不说这个。”那一句你念了两遍，因为他要你念。
# en: Read it plainly, then talk
opt.right.label [3ea1f4] = 平平地念，再聊聊
# en: You read it plainly. Then he talks about home for an hour, the farm, the frost, his mother alone at harvest, and you listen. It's a lot to carry. You carry some of it back with you.
opt.right.say.1 [bf92db] = 你平平地念完了。然后他讲了一个钟头的家：农场、霜、他母亲独自收割。你听着。这些很沉。你帮他带回了一些。
# en: When he gets to coming home after graduation, you ask what he wants, not what was planned. He doesn't know yet. He says nobody has asked him before.
opt.right.say.2 [f4871b] = 读到毕业后回家那一段，你问他想要什么，而不是原本计划好的是什么。他还不知道。他说以前从没有人问过他。

@event tobias_umbrella
# en: One Umbrella
title [e864cd] = 一把伞
# en: It's pouring, and Tobias has the biggest umbrella you've ever seen: patched, green, and older than both of you. {~"Ma's," he says. "It's seen worse."|"Room for two," he says, "or four, if they're small."}
text [44b417] = 大雨倾盆，托比亚斯有一把你见过的最大的伞：打着补丁，绿色的，比你们俩加起来还老。{~“我妈的，”他说，“它见过更糟的。”|“能挤两个人，”他说，“要是个子小，能挤四个。”}
# en: Two students walking close under one enormous patched umbrella across a rainy castle courtyard, one much bigger than the other.
scene [68b8fa] = 两个学生挤在一把巨大的补丁伞下穿过下雨的城堡庭院，一个比另一个高大得多。
# en: Walk close under it
opt.left.label [351a83] = 挤在伞下走
# en: {~You walk back under it, very close, because the umbrella insists, and your outside shoulder is soaked through by the door anyway. He tells you a long story about a goat that fell in a well, and you don't hear the end of it, and don't mind.|Halfway across the courtyard he stops talking. So do you. The rain does the talking, and runs down the back of your neck.}
opt.left.say.1 [384881] = {~你们挤在伞下走回去，挨得很近，因为伞执意如此，可到门口时你靠外的那边肩膀还是湿透了。他讲了一个山羊掉进井里的长故事，结尾你没听见，也不在乎。|走到庭院一半他不说话了。你也没说。雨替你们说，还顺着你的后颈往下淌。}
# en: Race him to the door
opt.right.label [d816e0] = 跟他赛跑到门口
# en: {~You run. He runs after you with the umbrella and arrives soaked anyway, laughing from the belly.|You make it first, drenched. He arrives dry and very pleased with himself.}
opt.right.say.1 [020d6d] = {~你跑了起来。他打着伞追你，到了还是湿透了，笑得肚子直颤。|你先到了，浑身湿透。他到的时候一身干爽，得意极了。}

@event tobias_seed_month
# en: A Seed a Month
title [f09a24] = 每月一颗种子
# en: Tobias gives you one seed a month, every month, in a twist of paper with its name on it. Your windowsill is crowded now. {~This month's is a sunflower. "For when it's grey," he says.|This month's is a herb you've never heard of. "For your cough," he says. You don't have a cough. "Yet," he says.}
text [a221eb] = 托比亚斯每个月给你一颗种子，每个月都给，包在一个写着名字的纸卷里。你的窗台已经挤满了。{~这个月是向日葵。“阴天的时候用。”他说。|这个月是一种你从没听说过的草药。“治你的咳嗽。”他说。你没咳嗽。“还没。”他说。}
# en: A large student pressing a single seed into a pot on a windowsill crowded with sprouting pots, another student watching.
scene [b60a91] = 一个高大的学生把一颗种子按进窗台上的花盆里，窗台挤满了发芽的小盆，另一个学生在旁边看着。
# en: Plant it together
opt.left.label [e4538b] = 一起种下
# en: {~You plant it together, his big hands over yours, pressing the soil down gently. He waters it. You'll remember this month by it.|He shows you how deep, how much water, where the light falls. The windowsill is a calendar now.}
opt.left.say.1 [6a75bb] = {~你们一起种下它，他的大手覆在你手上，轻轻压实土。他浇了水。你会靠它记住这个月。|他教你种多深、浇多少水、光从哪儿照进来。窗台现在是一本日历了。}
# en: Give him one back
opt.right.label [354d55] = 回送他一颗
# en: {~You buy a seed in the village and give it to him in a twist of paper. He holds it as if it were a jewel, and plants it that day.|You give him a seed back. He laughs from the belly and plants it in his best pot.}
opt.right.say.1 [9f214f] = {~你在镇上买了一颗种子，包在纸卷里送他。他捧着它像捧着一颗宝石，当天就种下了。|你回送他一颗种子。他笑得肚子直颤，把它种进了他最好的花盆里。}

@event tobias_home_or_here
# en: Home or Here
title [1957bb] = 回家，还是留下
# en: Tobias has been quiet all week. Finally: "Ma wants me home after. The farm. It's always been the plan." He doesn't look at you. "I always thought I wanted that. I'm sorry. I'm sorry for saying it like this. I'm sorry."
text [5855ce] = 托比亚斯一整个星期都很安静。终于他开口：“我妈想让我毕业后回家。回农场。一直都是这么打算的。”他不看你。“我一直以为我想要那样。对不起。对不起，这么说出来。对不起。”
# en: A large student sitting on a farm gate in a dream-like vision, then on a castle wall, torn between the two.
scene [4ca207] = 一个高大的学生在梦境般的画面里坐在农场的栅栏门上，又坐在城堡的墙头，在两者之间左右为难。
# en: "Then I'll come and see the goats."
opt.left.label [ba5ecb] = “那我去看山羊。”
# en: He looks up so fast he nearly falls off the wall. "You'd like the goats," he says. "They'd like you." Neither of you knows what comes after. It's enough, for now, that you'd come.
opt.left.say.1 [e92bfa] = 他猛地抬头，差点从墙上掉下去。“你会喜欢那些山羊的，”他说，“它们也会喜欢你。”你们谁都不知道之后会怎样。眼下，你愿意去，这就够了。
# en: "Do you still want it?"
opt.right.label [a987cf] = “你现在还想要吗？”
# en: He thinks for a long time, the way he thinks about seeds. "I don't know," he says at last. "I didn't know I was allowed not to know." You sit with him until he stops apologising.
opt.right.say.1 [36a49b] = 他想了很久，就像他琢磨种子那样。“我不知道，”他终于说，“我不知道我可以不知道。”你陪他坐着，直到他不再道歉。

@event tobias_gerald_wilts
# en: Gerald Is Ill
title [79d6f3] = 杰拉尔德病了
# en: Gerald is wilting. His hat has slipped, his leaves are grey, and he hasn't screamed in two days. Tobias is sitting on the greenhouse floor holding the pot, and he isn't apologising, which is how you know it's bad.
text [0a20fa] = 杰拉尔德蔫了。帽子滑到一边，叶子发灰，两天没叫一声。托比亚斯坐在温室地上抱着花盆，没有道歉——你就是从这一点看出事情严重了。
# en: A large student cradling a drooping potted mandrake in a knitted hat, sitting on a greenhouse floor, another student kneeling beside him.
scene [c1883c] = 一个高大的学生坐在温室地上，怀里抱着一盆戴毛线帽、垂头丧气的曼德拉草，另一个学生跪在他身边。
# en: Brew him a tonic
opt.left.label [edae25] = 给他熬一剂补药
# en: You brew all night. At dawn Gerald drinks it, shudders, and screams, loudly, furiously, beautifully. Tobias laughs and cries at once and holds you so hard your ribs creak.
opt.left.say.1 [2cab30] = 你熬了一整夜。黎明时杰拉尔德喝下去，打了个哆嗦，然后尖叫起来——响亮、愤怒、美妙极了。托比亚斯又哭又笑，把你抱得肋骨咯吱作响。
# en: The tonic does nothing. But in the morning Gerald is a little greener anyway, maybe because Tobias didn't sleep and neither did you. "It's not your fault," Tobias says. "It's nobody's. You stayed."
opt.left.say.2 [f78e5e] = 补药没起作用。可第二天早上杰拉尔德还是绿了一点，也许是因为托比亚斯没睡，你也没睡。“不是你的错，”托比亚斯说，“谁的错都不是。你留下来了。”
# en: Sit with him all night
opt.right.label [cb261a] = 陪他坐一整夜
# en: You sit on the greenhouse floor all night, Tobias holding Gerald, you holding Tobias. At dawn Gerald stirs, and screams, very softly. It's the best sound you've ever heard.
opt.right.say.1 [605705] = 你在温室地上坐了一整夜，托比亚斯抱着杰拉尔德，你抱着托比亚斯。黎明时杰拉尔德动了动，非常轻地尖叫了一声。那是你听过最好听的声音。

@event tobias_ex
# en: He Still Waters Your Plant
title [9d492e] = 他还在给你的花浇水
# en: You find Tobias at your window, watering the plant on your sill. He jumps. "Sorry," he says. "Sorry. It looked dry. I'll go. I'm sorry."
text [da1753] = 你发现托比亚斯在你窗前，给你窗台上的植物浇水。他吓了一跳。“对不起，”他说，“对不起。它看着有点干。我这就走。对不起。”
# en: A large student watering a single pot on a windowsill that isn't his, glancing guiltily at the door.
scene [183bc5] = 一个高大的学生在不属于他的窗台前给一盆花浇水，心虚地瞥向门口。
# en: Let him go
opt.left.label [75e63a] = 让他走
# en: He goes. The plant is very well watered. You don't know whether to be grateful or sad, so you're both.
opt.left.say.1 [525790] = 他走了。那盆植物被浇得足足的。你不知道该感激还是难过，于是两样都有。
# en: Ask him to stay a minute
opt.right.label [07b9a3] = 请他再待一会儿
# en: He stays. You talk about the plant, and then about goats, and it's almost easy. "Friends," he says, at the door, testing the word, "is a good word. I like it."
opt.right.say.1 [31388f] = 他留下了。你们聊那盆植物，又聊山羊，几乎是轻松的。“朋友，”他在门口说，试着念这个词，“是个好词。我喜欢。”
# en: He stays, and stands, and apologises four times, and goes. The plant turns toward the door after him.
opt.right.say.2 [b5bd8a] = 他留下了，站着，道了四次歉，走了。那盆植物朝着门口转过去，跟着他。

@event tobias_dance_specialized
# en: The Broom Waltz, Again
title [be6251] = 又是扫帚华尔兹
# en: Tobias has been practising again, he admits, with the broom. "It complained," he says. "But I'm better now. I think. Will you?" He holds out a hand the size of a spade, very carefully.
text [1aa5ca] = 托比亚斯承认，他又拿扫帚练过了。“它抱怨了，”他说，“不过我现在好些了。我想是吧。你愿意吗？”他伸出一只铁锹那么大的手，非常小心。
# en: A large student counting steps under his breath in a moonlit greenhouse, guiding another student between rows of plants.
scene [83793a] = 月光下的温室里，一个高大的学生低声数着舞步，引着另一个学生在一排排植物间穿行。
# en: Dance with him
opt.left.label [faa28e] = 和他跳舞
# en: He's better. He steps on your foot only twice, and apologises five times, and between the apologies he's a wonderful dancer, slow and sure, like a tide.
opt.left.say.1 [687404] = 他确实好些了。只踩了你的脚两次，道了五次歉，而在道歉之间，他是个很棒的舞伴，缓慢而稳当，像潮水。
# en: Teach him a new step
opt.right.label [ea5169] = 教他一个新舞步
# en: You teach him a step from the Midwinter Ball. He gets it on the ninth try and is so proud he dances it alone, between the tomato plants, until the gardener throws him out.
opt.right.say.1 [59867f] = 你教他一个仲冬舞会上的舞步。他第九次学会了，得意得在番茄架之间独自跳起来，直到园丁把他赶出去。

@event tobias_friend_sick
# en: Too Big for the Bed
title [e13df4] = 床太小了
# en: Tobias has Lake Fever, and the infirmary bed is a foot too short for him. His feet stick out at the end under a blanket. He isn't worried about himself. "Gerald," he croaks. "Who's watering Gerald?"
text [44a27e] = 托比亚斯得了湖热病，医务室的床比他短一英尺。他的脚从毯子底下伸出床尾。他不担心自己。“杰拉尔德，”他哑着嗓子说，“谁给杰拉尔德浇水？”
# en: A very large student squeezed into a small infirmary bed, feet hanging off the end, a potted mandrake on the bedside table.
scene [341399] = 一个非常高大的学生挤在医务室的小床上，脚伸出床尾，床头柜上放着一盆曼德拉草。
# en: Send a card, and a promise
opt.left.label [44b1dd] = 寄张卡片，许个承诺
# en: You send a card with a drawing of Gerald in a sickbed hat. Tobias keeps it propped against the water jug and shows it to Sister Amaranth twice a day.
opt.left.say.1 [f92992] = 你寄了张卡片，上面画着戴病号帽的杰拉尔德。托比亚斯把它靠在水壶上，一天给阿玛兰斯修女看两遍。
# en: Water Gerald, and sit with him
opt.right.label [3b6f2c] = 给杰拉尔德浇水，陪着他
# en: You water Gerald, then sit with Tobias every evening until he's better. Then you're in the next bed. Tobias waters Gerald for both of you, apologising to everyone.
opt.right.say.1 [d3220c] = 你给杰拉尔德浇水，然后每晚陪着托比亚斯，直到他好起来。然后你躺进了隔壁那张床。托比亚斯替你们俩给杰拉尔德浇水，见谁都道歉。
# en: {~You bring Gerald to the infirmary in his pot. Amaranth objects. Gerald screams at her. Tobias recovers mostly from laughing.|You water Gerald every morning and report on him every evening, leaf by leaf. Tobias gets better, he says, out of relief.|You read him farming almanacs aloud until he falls asleep, which takes four pages. He recovers in three days.}
opt.right.say.2 [3e178f] = {~你把杰拉尔德连盆带到医务室。阿玛兰斯反对。杰拉尔德冲她尖叫。托比亚斯主要是笑好的。|你每天早上给杰拉尔德浇水，每晚汇报它的情况，一片叶子一片叶子地讲。托比亚斯说他是放下心来才好的。|你给他念农事历书，念到第四页他就睡着了。三天后他就好了。}

@event lyra_teach_spell
# en: A Trick Worth Learning
title [8a5e67] = 值得一学的小把戏
# en: Lyra doesn't invent little spells. "Half-useful is useless," she says. But she'll teach you the flourish her family has used to open a duel for two hundred years, if you swear not to tell anyone she taught it to someone outside the family. She looks as if she might regret the offer.
text [9d32e0] = 莱拉不发明小咒语。“半有用就是没用。”她说。不过她愿意教你她家两百年来决斗开场用的起手式，前提是你发誓不告诉任何人她教给了外人。她看上去随时可能后悔。
# en: A duelling hall after hours, a red-haired girl correcting another student's wand arm with two fingers, a scorched practice target behind them.
scene [fb3422] = 下课后的决斗厅，一个红发女孩用两根手指纠正另一个学生持杖的手臂，身后是一个烧焦的练习靶。
# en: Learn it her way
opt.left.label [0555fe] = 照她的方法学
# en: She corrects your wrist eleven times. On the twelfth the flourish leaves a ribbon of flame in the air, exactly where it should be. Lyra nods once. "Adequate," she says, which from her is a medal.
opt.left.say.1 [5c3f46] = 她纠正了你的手腕十一次。第十二次，起手式在空中留下一道火焰缎带，分毫不差。莱拉点了一下头。“还行。”她说——从她嘴里说出来，这是一枚勋章。
# en: The ribbon of flame goes where it shouldn't, which is your sleeve. Lyra puts it out with a flick and doesn't laugh, which is worse. "Again," she says. The second time it works.
opt.left.say.2 [0d5525] = 火焰缎带飞到了不该去的地方，也就是你的袖子上。莱拉一弹指把火灭了，没笑，这更糟。“再来。”她说。第二次成功了。
# en: Teach her to make toast
opt.right.label [7c8623] = 教她烤面包
# en: You hand her a slice of bread and a toasting fork. She looks at it the way she looks at a duelling opponent. Four slices are cinders. The fifth is golden. She eats it standing up, in silence, and then says, "Don't tell anyone that either."
opt.right.say.1 [a12bca] = 你递给她一片面包和一把烤叉。她看着它，就像看一个决斗对手。四片烤成了炭。第五片金黄。她站着默默吃完，然后说：“这件事也别告诉任何人。”
# en: You offer to trade: her flourish for something useful, like toast. She goes very still. "I can incinerate a target at forty paces," she says. "I cannot make toast." By the fifth slice she can. She makes you swear about that too.
opt.right.say.2 [171e99] = 你提议交换：她的起手式换个有用的东西，比如烤面包。她一下子僵住了。“我能在四十步外把靶子烧成灰，”她说，“我不会烤面包。”到第五片她会了。她让你也为这件事发了誓。
